From f33b4d97891f97e69fce5f74ec06a6c572ac96a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:42:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 397/406] Unified: design check: pairs that overlap on purpose,
 and parts turned through their motion

--ignore-pairs pairs.txt (A, B a line; labels or names of parts or their
groups, * and ?) and DesignCheck.allow_overlap(a, b), kept in the file;
ignoring an overlap in the panel now ignores that pair only, not the
rule for both parts. --sweep motion.json (DesignCheck.sweep): the parts
named are turned about an axis by steps and checked against the others
at each angle; exit code 1 on a hit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
